### Orvexa API v1 — journey step 05: SIGNED provider webhook
### POST /api/v1/webhooks/{provider} is PUBLIC but HMAC-verified and
### fail-closed: nothing unverified is persisted as processed.
###
### HOW THE SIGNATURE IS COMPUTED (platform scheme — any provider without a
### registered carrier verifier; exactly what scripts/e2e-demo.sh does):
###
###     X-Orvexa-Signature: hex(HMAC-SHA256(ORVEXA_SECRET, rawBody))
###
### e2e-demo.sh helper (source of truth for the math):
###
###     SIG=$(printf '%s' "$BODY" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "$ORVEXA_SECRET" -hex | awk '{print $2}')
###
### 1. Hash the EXACT raw body bytes below (a one-byte difference rejects).
###    For the single-line body used here:
###
###    printf '%s' '{"event":"message.delivered","interaction_id":"<ID from step 04>","tenant_id":"<TenantID from step 04>","detail":"delivered to handset"}' \
###      | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "$ORVEXA_SECRET" -hex | awk '{print $2}'
###
### 2. Export it and send:  export ORVEXA_WEBHOOK_SIG=<hex>
###
### Server config: ORVEXA_WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET must equal ORVEXA_SECRET.
### Carrier-registered providers verify differently instead (twilio:
### X-Twilio-Signature HMAC-SHA1 over url+fields; whatsappcloud [exact registry
### key] : X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=<hex(HMAC-SHA256(appSecret, rawBody))>;
### africastalking: peer-IP allowlist) — docs/runbooks/operations.md.
###
### The payload contract (internal/comms): event ∈ call.ringing|call.connected|
### call.ended|call.wrapup|call.failed|message.sent|message.delivered|
### message.wrapup|message.read|message.failed, interaction_id = platform
### interaction UUID, tenant_id = tenant UUID. The event drives a guarded
### lifecycle transition on that interaction.

@ORVEXA_URL = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_URL}}
@ORVEXA_WEBHOOK_SIG = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_WEBHOOK_SIG}}

### Signed delivery → 202 Accepted {event_id, duplicate:false, processed:true}
# @name signedWebhook
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/webhooks/whatsapp_cloud
Content-Type: application/json
X-Orvexa-Signature: {{ORVEXA_WEBHOOK_SIG}}

{"event":"message.delivered","interaction_id":"REPLACE_WITH_INTERACTION_ID","tenant_id":"REPLACE_WITH_TENANT_ID","detail":"delivered to handset"}

###

### Replay the SAME delivery → 200 {event_id: <original>, duplicate:true}
### Idempotency is keyed on the raw body — replays are single-effect.
# @name signedWebhookReplay
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/webhooks/whatsapp_cloud
Content-Type: application/json
X-Orvexa-Signature: {{ORVEXA_WEBHOOK_SIG}}

{"event":"message.delivered","interaction_id":"REPLACE_WITH_INTERACTION_ID","tenant_id":"REPLACE_WITH_TENANT_ID","detail":"delivered to handset"}

###

### Unsigned delivery → 401 webhook.invalid_signature (fail-closed, nothing
### persisted as processed — no unsigned ingestion path exists)
# @name unsignedWebhookRejected
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/webhooks/whatsapp_cloud
Content-Type: application/json

{"event":"message.delivered","interaction_id":"REPLACE_WITH_INTERACTION_ID","tenant_id":"REPLACE_WITH_TENANT_ID"}
